---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Doodle from '../components/Doodle.astro';
import { SITE_DEFAULT_DESCRIPTION, SITE_HOME_TITLE } from '../data/site-meta';

const modules = import.meta.glob('../data/lessons/*.json', { eager: true });
const lessons = Object.values(modules)
	.map((m) => m.default ?? m)
	.sort((a, b) => a.number.localeCompare(b.number));
---
<Base title={`AI410 | ${SITE_HOME_TITLE}`} description={SITE_DEFAULT_DESCRIPTION}>
	<header class="masthead home-hero">
		<div class="home-stage" aria-hidden="true">
			<span class="orbit orbit-a"></span>
			<span class="orbit orbit-b"></span>
			<span class="orbit orbit-c"></span>
			<span class="sci sci-walk float-a"><Doodle kind="walker" /></span>
			<span class="sci sci-sat float-b"><Doodle kind="sat" /></span>
			<span class="sci sci-rocket float-c"><Doodle kind="rocket" /></span>
			<span class="sci sci-planet float-d"><Doodle kind="planet" /></span>
			<span class="sci sci-ufo float-e"><Doodle kind="ufo" /></span>
			<span class="scrap scrap-sticky scrap-3 float-c">10</span>
			<span class="doodle doodle-star">★</span>
			<span class="doodle doodle-star doodle-star-2">★</span>
			<span class="doodle doodle-star doodle-star-3">✦</span>
			<svg class="doodle doodle-scribble" viewBox="0 0 120 36" fill="none">
				<path d="M4 22c18-16 28 14 46 2 16-10 22 12 42-4 12-10 22 6 24 8" />
			</svg>
		</div>

		<div class="hero-copy">
			<p class="kicker reveal">ai410</p>
			<h1 class="reveal delay-1">How AI systems <span class="flip">actually work</span>.</h1>
			<p class="byline reveal delay-2">By <a href="/who/">Adler Archer</a></p>
			<p class="dek reveal delay-3">
				Plain-language explanations of the parts that matter, written by someone who builds with
				these systems in federal permitting.
			</p>
		</div>
	</header>

	<main class="home-start">
		<p>
			A model knows what it read while it was being taught, plus whatever you paste into the chat.
			It does not know your inbox, your company's records, or what a permitting database says today.
			Those things were never in the lesson. A fluent answer about them is still a guess.
		</p>
		<p>
			If you want it to see something current, you fetch text and hand it over. Search, a document, a
			row from a live system. That is retrieval. The model reads what it is given. Nothing is sent,
			booked, or filed.
		</p>
		<p>
			If you want it to do something, it calls a function that runs somewhere else. That is tool use.
			A tool can look up which flights are left on Tuesday. It can also book one. Those two sentences
			feel the same and are not. Doing things has consequences that reading does not, which is why a
			careful demo is read-only on purpose.
		</p>
		<p>
			MCP, when it shows up, is only the plug on the doing job. It is not the capability. The plug
			does not decide read versus write. Someone has to.
		</p>

		<div class="contents">
			{lessons.map((lesson) => (
				<a class="entry" href={`/lessons/${lesson.slug}/`}>
					<span class="num">{lesson.number}</span>
					<div>
						<h2>{lesson.title}</h2>
						<p>{lesson.blurb}</p>
					</div>
				</a>
			))}
		</div>
	</main>
</Base>
